dpyright | 0 new warnings (804 → 791); 1 error, same as baseline |\n| pytest on the resilience file | 146 passed |\n| unittest discover on `/usr/bin/python3` 3.9.6 | 146 OK |\n| `tests/test_images_strict.py` | 18 passed |\n| AST gates (VER-007, VER-009) | pass, all 40 QA ids covered |\n| scope and frozen-hash check (VER-008) | passes on the working tree |\n\n- **VER-008 as written** uses `git diff --name-only BASE HEAD`, so it can only pass after the three files are committed. I ran the same assertions against the working tree.\n- **basedpyright error:** its one error is already in the baseline, at an existing test line `[uri, uri + \"&immutable=1\"]`. I couldn't touch it because existing test lines had to stay unmodified.\n\nWhat the server now does with images:\n- **Off by default.** Images are accepted only when the flag is on and the model's proof matches (binary SHA-256, method version, formats, effort); text-only requests are unaffected.\n- **Validation before the queue.** Count and size are checked before any decode, and nothing is written to disk until a slot is acquired.\n- **Staging after the slot.** The flag and proof are re-checked there; files then go in a 0700/0600 `img-<uuid>` directory that lives for all retries and is removed in `finally`.\n- **Prompts and CLI.** Images get global `[image N]` numbers, and a resumed prompt lists only the new images. The CLI gets `--add-dir`; cwd and the session key are untouched.\n- **Cleanup and logging.** A sweep deletes orphaned dirs but skips active ones and symlinks. The reject-reason log tokens are unmasked, and the model name is sanitized in logs.\n\nI checked the tests can fail: six deliberate breakages of the server each made at least one test fail.\n\nDeviations (full list in `plans/coder-01.json`):\n- **Model names.** The repo's four other models are `gemini-3.7-flash`, `gemini-3.6-flash`, `gemini-3.1-pro` and `gpt-oss-120b`, not the names in the brief. I left them untouched as text-only. The two targets also get `cli_registry: implicit_supported`, because the catalog rejects `explicit_unsupported` on a non-unsupported model.\n- **Existing names kept.** I used `DYNAMIC_CONFIG_PATH` and `AGY_BIN`, which already exist, and wrote `IMPLEMENTED_METHODS` as a plain assignment because VER-009 only inspects plain assignments.\n- **Architecture over brief.** A string `image_url` and an empty base64 payload follow the approved architecture (AD-002) and are rejected as invalid, not accepted as the brief says.\n- **No decoded bytes held (F-004).** Validation keeps only the base64, and staging decodes after the slot.\n- **Small-limit tests.** The boundary tests patch the size limits down, because real 20 MiB payloads pushed process RSS past the existing 112 MiB test. The real limit constants are asserted in `test_ao10`.\n- **Validator command lines.** `validate_role_plan.py` has no `--role` or `--before` flags, and `validate_handoff.py` needs `--role-plan` and cannot be run with `-I`; I ran them in the forms they accept.\n\nOpen risks:\n- **Proof values.** The fleet proof (low/medium/high efforts, four formats) is the target state the brief asked for, but only PNG on Argon at low effort was proven live. `IMAGE_INPUT_ENABLED` must stay false in the runtime config until the L2/L3 matrix passes.\n- **Env override.** `AGY_IMAGE_INPUT_ENABLED=1` enables images by itself, per the brief; nothing sets it in `start.sh`.\n- **Memory (RES-01).** Queued image requests keep roughly twice the base64 size in memory until staging; this is not measured.\n- **Validation depth.** Validation checks the file signature only, so a corrupted image with a valid magic header is accepted.\n\nFiles are in `.ai-team/runs/agy-image-input-fix-20261029/`:\n- plans/coder-01.before.json\n- plans/coder-01.json\n- handoffs/coder-01.json\n- coder.json\n\nBoth plan and handoff validate.","ttft_ms":2742,"type":"result","duration_ms":1658290,"uuid":"d411f295-83fe-4df4-89ed-626b7af91515","ttft_stream_ms":2244,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":2244,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
